    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "ArchiMate models — every view, element and relationship a node",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-09: *\"need new specialixed harness (like openapi) for archimate\ncontent in the KG\"*, and then, of the Archi CLI report: *\"do not do java\n200mb... that's not usable for webclients and is too heavy.\"*",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Readable page paths: slugs, worked out each build",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-30, of `…/views/id-007936f8c2424b96ad1893ef0ff66059/`: *\"do\nwe need to use such ugly IDs … why not nicer slug IRIs?\"*; then, of the\ndesigns offered\n([issue 1054](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/1054)):\n*\"B. clean break ok\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "issues/1054",
        "2026-10-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Readable page paths: slugs, worked out each build",
      "prov:value": "**The IRI stays the id; only the page is at a slug.** A view's or element's\npage is at `<m>/views/1-central-health-workforce-registry/`, while its node\nkeeps `<m>/views/<id>.jsonld`. Cite the IRI when a link must last: the page\npath is for reading. Relationships keep id paths, since almost none are\nnamed (smart-ra 0.2.0: 6 of 284)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Readable page paths: slugs, worked out each build",
      "prov:value": "- a rename moves the page, and the old path is gone (a clean break, as the\n  owner chose; old `<m>/views/<id>/` page paths are gone too);\n- on a clash the object first in the model keeps the plain slug and a later\n  one gets `-<first hex of its id>`;\n- an author can choose a slug in Archi with a `slug` property (lower-case\n  words joined by `-`); a malformed one, or two objects choosing the same\n  one, is refused rather than rewritten;\n- an object with no readable name keeps its id as its path."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The metamodel is derived, never drawn",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-31: *\"i dont really like native UML, rather derived\"*, then\n*\"make mechanical tools as parts of skills/processes\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The metamodel is derived, never drawn",
      "prov:value": "`archimate-metamodel --check` fails when a relationship follows a pattern\nArchiMate does not allow. Placeholders are reported, never fatal: a model is\nits authors', so removing a hand-drawn metamodel view (smart-ra 0.2.0's\n\"Metamodel\", \"Metamodel vs EIRA\" and \"Testing\", 34 placeholders) is their\ncall. Cite the derived page instead of the view in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Actors come first; the model points at them",
      "prov:value": "smart-ra#166 D4, owner's choice of 2026-11-01. The SMART Guidelines order is\nfixed: a DAK's L2 generic personas become the IG's L3 FHIR ActorDefinitions,\nand the architecture realizes them (DPI-H RA §4.3.2). So **the ActorDefinitions\nare written in the IG, from the DAK personas, and the model only points at\nthem.** A model author tags the box that realizes an actor in Archi with the\nproperty `fhir-actor`, whose value is the actor's canonical URL\n(`fhir-actor = http://smart.who.int/ra/ActorDefinition/FacilityRegistry`), the\nsame way an element carries `skosConcept`.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "smart-ra#166",
        "2026-11-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "A document's tables and figures are drawn, not typed",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-01 (smart-ra, cards Q-RAC-1 B and Q-RAC-2 A, \"the rules stay\nin charge\"): a table or figure in the document that restates the model is\ngenerated from data by the Tool `archimate-blocks`, and `--check` keeps it\nfrom drifting.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Untangle every view you touch",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-31, of a view with lines drawn across each other and through\nboxes: *\"lots crossed lines. detangle. (skill/process always check and try\nminimize when authoring archimate)\"*, then *\"improve skills / make mechanical\ntools where you can\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every view carries a key for readers who do not know ArchiMate",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-31: *\"what do arrows/colors/shapes mean, need legend\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "Every view carries a key for readers who do not know ArchiMate",
      "prov:value": "Readers of a view are mostly not architects. **Every rendered view carries a\nplain-language key** below it, saying what each colour, shape, line and end\nused ON THAT VIEW means, in words a reader without ArchiMate understands\n(\"Realization: makes real, or achieves\"), not the specification's terms\nalone. `render-view.ts` draws it by default\n([pull 1059](https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/pull/1059)), keyed\nonly to what the view uses. Do not turn it off for a published view, and do\nnot export a view without it. When the renderer gains a new mark, the key\ngains its line in the same change.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "pull/1059"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Names are the source's own terms, linked to their concept",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-31, after an NHWA element was named in our words rather than\nthe handbook's (smart-ra#163).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "smart-ra#163",
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The model is never a source of the glossary",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-11-02: *\"i dont want ArchiMate to be source of SKOS (unless it\nwas ingested)\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-11-02"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-11-02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Versions — one folder per SemVer version",
      "prov:value": "A model is named for the version of the thing it describes. In a WHO IG\nrepository that is the `version:` in `sushi-config.yaml`: `archimate/0.2.0/`,\nwith earlier drafts as SemVer pre-releases (`0.2.0-draft.1`, …). The model id\nin the config is that version, so `…/archimate/0.2.0/elements/<id>.jsonld` is\nboth versioned and stable. Never name a folder `v2`, `prev1` or `current`: a\nlabel that says nothing about what it is a version of is how smart-ra came to\nhold two byte-identical models under two names."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "In a folio's build",
      "prov:value": "Run both in the staging build, after the document site is built and before\nthe navbar pass, so the pages are railed like every other page. `--out` is\nthe normal mode: smart-ra's four models are 5,809 pages and 131 drawings\n(~24 MB, 1.5 s), which belong in a build, not a commit.\n`gen-archimate-pages.ts` without `--out` writes into the graph and `--check`\ngates it, as the `openapi` subgraph does, for an instance small enough to\ncommit its pages."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Citing the model from prose",
      "prov:value": "Link the element's or the view's page, never a copy of a picture. A view's\nSVG links relative to its own address, so it can also be embedded in a\ndocument as a figure (`<m>/views/<id>.svg`) and stay current with the model.\nWhere the document and the model disagree — a figure in the text that is not\na view in the model — that is a finding for the model's authors, not\nsomething to paper over with an exported image. (smart-ra, 2026-10-09:\nFigures 3.7.1 and 3.7.2 of the DPI-H review draft were in no committed model;\nthe 0.2.0 model now draws them as views \"B\" and \"D\", so cite those.)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-09"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
